※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4456

※ An array either carries its shape in the type, and then needs no room beyond
※ its elements, or carries the whole of it beside the elements.  Half of each
※ would be a value whose parts depend on which half is which.

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let m: u8⟦2,⟧ = ⟦⟦1u8⟧,⟦2u8⟧⟧
    m⟦0,0⟧
